title REDS %734's free half -- the census of Rishi refusals that discard the reason, and the cohort that left it unreadable
prompt fleet lap; the prior lap committed the %788 census and never pushed, so the send came first, then reds first took the half of an OPEN row no word is waiting on
rota lap 5227, row 2 -- Fire, the row that sees; cut and stop. Standfast says root rather than symptom, and %734's root is a compiler-bridge decision wanting Keaton's word -- yet the row names a SECOND fault, free, that nothing in the tree could see.
think The prior lap's work stood committed and unpushed -- round-open read ahead by 1. A lap ends at the commit and a round ends at the send, so the witness ran GREEN again on metal and both remotes took it before anything new opened.
think %734 is OPEN and its repair is Keaton's. Reading it through fire rather than around it: ten of its thirteen captured failures carried their own reason and identified the cause; three said only Lattice build failed. The cause is gated; the SILENCE is not.
think Every Rishi .ok comes from a record the interpreter builds at rishi/src/main.rye:1563 with six named fields, err and err_brief among them. So the evidence exists at every one of these sites and the cure is one interpolation the tree already writes 1,708 times.
think Measured before claiming: 10,234 asserts on a run record over 2,571 tracked sources. 1,708 name their own err, 462 the wrong stream, 550 a file on disk, 31 a say line above, 7,483 nothing at all. On build asserts alone the split is 744 cured against 720 mute -- half the tree applies a cure the other half omits.
think The binding reading nearly lied. A first pass traced only run [ and called 183 sites unbound; following a locally defined fn one level -- fn git-run tail: run (...) -- and telling run-bounded from run brought that to 82, of which 80 are genuinely path-shaped records with no err field at all.
obs The scan ran 20.4 seconds as one awk process per file and 3.3 as one pass over all of them, with identical readings. A lap-tier guard on eight ships pays that difference every lap.
obs The strongest leg is the one that runs the two forms rather than reading them. A mute refusal prints four constant words; the cured one prints `Lattice build failed -- unable to load pan.zig`, which is the exact sentence %734 spent a fortnight unable to read.
obs Two control legs failed first and both were my plants rather than the scan. A conditional binding holding a literal run [ IS seen, so the unseen plant had to call a named function; and a mutation removing the say SHAPE test bites only where an earlier non-say line names the record. Mutate the half that carries the weight.
obs The sweep took the 80 sites %734 names and nothing else. Proven a pure append off the diff: 80 pairs, each the elder message plus the record's own err_brief, zero lines otherwise changed. mute 7,483 to 7,403, names_err 1,708 to 1,788, ceiling lowered in the same commit.
obs Two inherited reds met and neither is mine: the roster reads runs_red=18 which the card already accounts for, and pen_release reads never_removed=9 against a ceiling of 8, unmoved by my two pen-carrying files. Both proven by stashing this lap's work and re-reading.
obs The card refused the first commit at 14 bytes over its bound, and its opening paragraph was a two-day-old reading of sixteen OPEN rows. Counting status markers under their own row headers answers twelve OPEN and one BOOKED, and the true sentence is 36 bytes shorter than the stale one.
